# commands.words - Dingus Quest Zero's words, for what a command means to the game: the parser (games/dq0c, dq0c.s)
# makes the game's command (hub.h's struct cmd) by them and the verbs (commands.verbs: each verb's words, its actions),
# from the words of a line the grammar (commands.ebnf) has taken, and sim/tools/commandwords.js does the same on the
# host (the tests' reference).  They began as the old parser's tables (games/dq0/parse.c, 2026-10-19), word for word;
# what changed is marked "(new)".
#
# A section a kind of word; a line a word (or words) = its meaning, the names dq0.h, hub.h and level.h give (OR_*,
# H_*, OB_*, PR_*, HOW_*, SL_*).  A word is looked for as it was typed, then as the root its alias gives
# (commands.aliases), so an alias the player makes means what its root means.
#   [orders]   a request to an ally (an order's: the first)
#   [dirs]     a way: by the compass (H_*), as the character faces (REL n: an eighth turn n), GO_UP, GO_DOWN; two
#              together are the way between them
#   [things]   a kind of thing it can see (OB_*); PART: a part of one, its own word the thing's word too
#   [preps]    after the first thing, the other's: in it, on it, from it
#   [how]      up to it (HOW_TO) or through it (HOW_THROUGH)
#   [special]  words the meaning turns on: WITH (the other thing, used: whatever came before), WAY_OUT (the way out),
#              AWAY (put away: stowed), BACK (put back: not a way), HALF (a half turn), AROUND (turned or looked
#              round), BAR (put the bar ...: barred)
#   [selectors] which of several things the thing is (SL_*: the closest, the second, all of them; it, the last thing
#              named) (new)
#   [little]   passed over

